== Results ==
Incumbent president [[Zoran Milanović]] won a second term in office with 75% of the vote, the highest for a presidential candidate in Croatia, not counting president [[Franjo Tuđman]]'s first round victories in [[1992 Croatian presidential election|1992]] and [[1997 Croatian presidential election|1997]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=13 January 2025 |title=Croatia populist president re-elected in landslide |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20250112-croatia-s-populist-president-appears-set-for-re-election |access-date=13 January 2025 |website=[[France 24]]|language=en}}</ref>

According to political analysts, HDZ likely expected Primorac to win 30&ndash;40% of the second-round vote after only winning 19% in the first round;<ref>{{cite web |title=Komunikolozi se slažu: Primorac jučer nije napravio dovoljno. HDZ se priprema za poraz, očekuju pobjedu Milanovića od 60 do 70 posto |url=https://www.telegram.hr/politika-kriminal/komunikolozi-se-slazu-primorac-jucer-nije-napravio-dovoljno-hdz-se-priprema-za-poraz-ocekuju-pobjedu-milanovica-od-60-do-70-posto/ |website=Telegram.hr |access-date=16 January 2025 |language=hr |date=8 January 2025}}</ref> however, Milanović likely attracted a number of HDZ voters.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Redžić |first1=Dea |title=Puhovski: Milanović je nezakoniti politički sin Franje Tuđmana, Plenković je izgubio dodir s realnošću |url=https://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/puhovski-milanovic-je-nezakoniti-politicki-sin-franje-tudmana-plenkovic-izgubio-dodir-s-realnoscu-1830057 |website=Večernji list |access-date=16 January 2025 |language=hr |date=13 January 2025}}</ref> The results of the second round were taken as a sign of a small loyal voter base for the HDZ, since the large point difference in the first round likely demotivated voters. Some blamed Primorac's low vote count on a poor choice of candidate by the HDZ or the choice to initially campaign as an independent candidate before the formal HDZ endorsement.<ref name="bagic">{{cite web |last1=Balija |first1=Petra |last2=Tokić |first2=Tea |title=Analitičari: Primorčev govor je skandalozan. Nije skupio niti malo dostojanstva da čestita pobjedniku |url=https://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/uskoro-uzivo-pratite-drugi-krug-izbora-uz-vecernji-tv-analiticari-ce-komentirati-odlazimo-i-u-stozere-1829756 |website=Večernji list |access-date=16 January 2025 |language=hr |date=12 January 2025}}</ref> Primorac and Prime Minister [[Andrej Plenković]] caused a minor controversy by not congratulating Milanović in their election night speeches;<ref name="bagic"/><ref>{{cite web |title=Dragan Primorac tvrdi da je čestitao Zoranu Milanoviću: 'On je građanin Hrvatske' |url=https://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/dragan-primorac-tvrdi-da-je-cestitao-zoranu-milanovicu-on-je-gradanin-hrvatske-1830091 |website=Večernji list |access-date=16 January 2025 |language=hr |date=13 January 2025}}</ref> though former president [[Kolinda Grabar-Kitarović]]<ref name="kgk">{{cite web |title=Kolindu ne interesira stav bivše stranke: potvrdila da dolazi na Milanovićevu inauguraciju |url=https://slobodnadalmacija.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/kolindu-ne-interesira-stav-bivse-stranke-potvrdila-da-dolazi-na-milanovicevu-inauguraciju-1446925 |website=[[Slobodna Dalmacija]] |access-date=16 January 2025 |location=Split |language=hr |date=14 January 2025}}</ref> and [[Archbishop of Zagreb]] [[Dražen Kutleša]] both congratulated him afterward.<ref name="kutlesa">{{cite web |title=Nadbiskup Kutleša čestitao Milanoviću, nahvalio ga: 'Vaš put je obilježen istaknutim i odgovornim služenjem' |url=https://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/nadbiskup-kutlesa-cestitao-milanovicu-nahvalio-ga-vas-put-je-obiljezen-istaknutim-i-odgovornim-sluzenjem-1830335 |website=Večernji list |access-date=16 January 2025 |location=Zagreb |language=hr |date=14 January 2025}}</ref>

